# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything listed here stays on the workstation.
#
# The rule: this repo holds the harness and the dashboard as SOURCE. It does
# not hold captured state - not another tool's credentials, not session
# transcripts, not machine-specific handoff notes. Those are reproducible or
# private; source is neither.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Pre-change snapshots. The grok-*.tar.gz archives in here are copies of the
# xAI CLI's entire state directory and each one contains .grok/auth.json, i.e.
# live credentials, plus session transcripts. Never publish.
# Dated pre-change snapshots. A glob, so the next one is covered without an edit.
.backup-*/

# Agent audit and hardening journals. Full of machine-local paths and
# credential-shaped strings that cannot be classified automatically.
audit_2026-09-17/
wsl-agent-teams/

# Internal handoff notes: machine layout, resume state, incident write-ups.
# Valuable on this box, wrong thing to publish.
ANALYSIS_2026-09-18.md
PENDING_USER_ACTION.md
RESUME.md
STATUS_CCC_*.md
TODO_next_demo.md
dashboard/BRIEF_*.md
dashboard/REVIEW_*.md

# Orchestration run artifacts. A brief is an instruction to a specific set of live
# agents and a result is that run's output; both are scratch from one machine's
# session, not source, and they land in the repo root only because that is the cwd
# the agents are parked on.
ORCHESTRATION_BRIEF.md
ORCHESTRATION_RESULT.md

# Scratch working area for a single run's artifacts (briefs, generated output).
# Same rule as the orchestration files above: run output, not source.
.penguin/

# Superseded copies kept beside the originals while refactoring.
*.bak
*.pre-*
*.baseline-run1

# Interpreter and editor leftovers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Runtime state and logs belong in ~/.agentmux, never here.
#
# .agentmux/agents/ in THIS repo is the exception, and it is not runtime state:
# those are agent definitions, versioned with the code they know how to work on,
# the way .claude/agents/ is. Do not add it here - a repo-local roster that is
# not committed is a roster only one machine has.
*.log
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Scratch a dispatched worker was given to write in. The smoke card's evidence
# points here, so the directory is kept and its contents are not.
tmp/

# Vendor protocol manuals, fetched on demand. Freely downloadable from the
# vendor, but theirs to distribute - not ours to commit. docs/vendor/README.md
# carries the URLs so anyone can fetch the same document.
docs/vendor/*.pdf

# Browser-automation output and dashboard screenshots. Captured state, not
# source: the .yml files are accessibility-tree dumps of a running instance and
# a screenshot of a live dashboard can carry whatever was on screen at the time
# - agent names, a scanned plant segment, device MACs. This repo is public.
# Root-anchored, not a blanket *.png: dashboard/assets/ may legitimately need an
# image one day, and a rule that silently swallows it is worse than this one.
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# ── FINANCIAL ARTIFACTS ARE NEVER COMMITTED. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. ────────────
#
# gh repo view: controlLogix/CControlCenter, isPrivate: false. Phase 5 adds a
# brokerage session, and a push cannot be taken back - a file deleted afterwards
# stays in the history, and by then it has been cloned and indexed.
#
# These paths are ignored so that an artifact written there lands ignored rather
# than staged. dashboard/check_no_financial_artifacts.sh fails if these pins go
# missing, for the same reason the eol pins are checked: a guard that only looks
# at today's tree passes the moment someone removes it and before anyone looks
# again.
#
# WHERE THEY GO INSTEAD, and this is the half that has to be written down:
#   %LOCALAPPDATA%\agentmux\broker\   the Fidelity session, its profile, orders
#   $AGENTMUX_HOME/investing/         positions, balances, research state
# Both are outside the repo on purpose. See docs/investing-boundary.md.
investing/
broker/
research/sessions/
# NOT agentmux-broker/ itself - that is SOURCE, and the plan runs
# `pytest agentmux-broker/test_killswitch.py`. Ignoring the whole directory
# would have blocked the very code this boundary exists to guard, which is what
# the first version of this did. Only the places an artifact could land inside
# it are ignored; artifacts are supposed to live outside the repo entirely, and
# check_no_financial_artifacts.sh catches them by filename wherever they land.
agentmux-broker/profile/
agentmux-broker/captures/
agentmux-broker/*.jsonl

# Node. The workspace root hoists every package here - 121 MB, 239 packages -
# and this repo is PUBLIC. Untracked is not the same as ignored: one `git add -A`
# commits all of it, and it is not removable from history afterwards.
node_modules/
packages/*/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.playwright-mcp/
